Dear members of the CSE community,

Welcome to the October edition of CSE Connect. Here is a quick round-up
of last month and a look at what is coming up.

Highlights from September:
- A third-year team placed second at an inter-college coding contest.
- The open-source club merged its first batch of student contributions
  into the course lab toolkit.
- Faculty completed the revision of the elective list for the next
  academic year.

Upcoming this month:
- Guest talk on practical machine learning pipelines: Wednesday, 14
  October 2026, 15:00-16:00 IST, Seminar Hall B.
- Introduction to Version Control workshop: Saturday, 24 October 2026,
  10:00-13:00 IST, Computer Lab 2. Limited to 40 participants; register
  at the department office.

Reminders:
- Mid-semester examination guidelines are on the department notice
  board.
- Lost-and-found items from the labs are kept at the department office
  for two weeks.

Warm regards,
CSE Connect Editorial Team
Department of Computer Science and Engineering
--=_TW_ALT_398f99ed158b3626
